<p style="font-size:12px;color:#888;text-align:center">（Singpass authentication required for identity verification）</p>

<h3>About Singpass Authentication</h3>
<p>The SIA Cadet Portal uses <b>Singpass</b> (Singapore's national digital identity) for verification:</p>
<ol>
<li>Click the verification button above</li>
<li>You will be redirected to <b>singpass.gov.sg</b> (Singapore government's official identity portal)</li>
<li>Log in with your Singpass (or create one using your passport)</li>
<li>Grant the requested permissions</li>
<li>Complete the medical questionnaire and upload documents</li>
</ol>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#E3F2FD;padding:12px;border-radius:4px">
<b>Why Singpass instead of just uploading documents?</b> As a foreign applicant, Singpass allows us to verify your identity against Singapore government records (immigration records, past visits, work passes). This prevents fraudulent applications — the SIA Cadet Programme receives over 4,000 applications per year and identity fraud is a serious concern. If you don't have a Singpass account, you can create one using your passport number at the Singpass website. The offline_access permission allows the medical questionnaire (which takes 30-45 minutes) to be completed across multiple sessions without losing progress.
</p>

